/**
 * prophet10.js - Sequential Prophet-10 (Rev4) emulation: panel, programmer,
 * globals, keyboard and MIDI. Sound is generated by Prophet10Processor.js.
 *
 * The panel is laid out in the coordinate system of the front-panel drawing in
 * Sequential's Prophet-10 User's Guide (1 unit = 1 px at the 1868 px design
 * width) and scaled as a whole to fit the window, so every control keeps the
 * hardware's proportions.
 *
 * Hold-button functions (hold the first button, press the second; Shift-click
 * latches a button as "held" for mouse users, multi-touch works natively):
 *   UNISON + GROUP/BANK ......... unison voices 1-10 / CHd (chord) / Pu2 (poly unison)
 *   UNISON + PROGRAM 1-8 ........ unison detune 0-7
 *   keys held + UNISON .......... store chord memory (single key, unison off: clear)
 *   KEYBOARD (osc B) + GROUP/BANK key priority LO, LOr, LAS, LAr, Hi, Hir
 *   FREQ A (wheel-mod) + GROUP/BANK pitch-wheel range 1-12
 *   VELOCITY + GROUP/BANK ....... velocity amount;  AFTERTOUCH + GROUP/BANK: aftertouch amount
 *   REV + PROGRAM 1-8 ........... Q compensation amount (Globals row 3 set to PrG)
 *   PRESET + GROUP/BANK ......... normal / stack / split;  PRESET (tap) in stack/split: edit layer A/B
 *   key + PRESET + BANK ......... set split point;  PRESET + VOLUME: layer balance
 *   UNISON + PRESET ............. link layers;  RECORD + PRESET: basic program
 *   RECORD + GLOBALS ............ reset globals;  RECORD, then GLOBALS: compare
 *   BANK + GLOBALS .............. globals row 3;  GLOBALS + PROGRAM 1/2: OS version
 *   GLOBALS x3 .................. store the current program as the power-on default
 */

